hadiths[103]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22720","Hasan and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Ibn Luhayyah narrated to us, Abu Qabil narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri saying, Hajjaj said: From Abu Qabil, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Jublani narrated to me that he heard Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I would not love to have the world and what is in it for this verse: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah, indeed Allah forgives all sins, indeed He is the Forgiving, the Merciful. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what about one who associates partners? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent, then said: Except one who associates partners, three times."
"22721","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, Humayd al-Shami narrated to me from Sulayman al-Manbihi from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he traveled, the last of his farewell to people was Fatimah, and the first whom he would visit when he arrived was Fatimah. He said: So he arrived from one of his expeditions and came to her, and he was wiping over her door, and he saw on al-Hasan and al-Husayn two heart-shaped pendants of silver, so he turned back and did not enter upon her. When Fatimah saw that, she thought he did not enter upon her because of what he saw, so she tore the curtain and removed the two pendants from the two boys and cut them, so the two boys wept, and she divided it between them. So they went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from them and said: O Thawban, take this to the family of so-and-so, a household in Madinah, and buy for Fatimah a necklace of sinew and two bracelets of ivory, for these are my household, and I do not love that they consume their good things in their worldly life."
"22722","Ishaq ibn Isa and Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, and this is the hadith of Ishaq, they said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Rashid ibn Dawud al-Umluki from Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on one of his journeys: We are traveling by night, so let no rider of a difficult mount nor a weak one travel by night. So a man traveled by night on a difficult she-camel of his, so he fell and his thigh was crushed, and he died. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered prayer over him, then ordered a caller to call among the people: Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient one, Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient one, three times."
"22723","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us from Abu Ammar Shaddad from Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to finish his prayer, would seek forgiveness three times, then say: O Allah, You are Peace and from You is peace, blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."
"22724","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Asim from Abu al-Aliyah from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Who will guarantee for me one thing and I guarantee Paradise for him? Thawban said: I will. He said: Do not ask people, meaning anything. He said: Yes. He said: So he would not ask."
"22725","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir from al-Abbas ibn Salim al-Lakhmi who said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz sent to Abu Sallam al-Habashi, so he was carried to him by post, asking him about the Hawd. So he was brought to him and he asked him, so he said: I heard Thawban saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: My Hawd is from Aden to Amman of al-Balqa, its water whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, and its cups are the number of stars. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst after it. The first people to come to it are the poor Muhajirun. So Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: They are disheveled in heads, dirty in clothes, who do not marry luxurious women, nor are the doors of nobility opened for them. So Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: I have married luxurious women and doors have been opened for me, unless Allah has mercy on me. By Allah, I shall not oil my head until it is disheveled, nor wash my garment next to my body until it becomes dirty."
"22726","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us from his book, Ibn Luhayyah narrated to us, a shaykh narrated to us from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever kills a young or an old one, or burns a palm tree, or cuts a fruitful tree, or slaughters a sheep for its skin, will not return even."
"22727","Affan narrated to us, Hammam and Aban narrated to us, they said: Qatadah narrated to us from Salim from Madan from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever the soul leaves the body while he is free of three enters Paradise: arrogance, debt, and misappropriation of spoils."
"22728","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad who said: It was said to Thawban: Narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: You tell lies against me. And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim prostrates to Allah a prostration except Allah raises him a degree by it, or removes a sin from him by it."
"22729","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"22730","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abu al-Judi from Balj from Abu Shaybah al-Mahri, who was the storyteller of the people in Constantinople, who said: It was said to Thawban: Narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomit and break the fast."
"22731","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a Muslim man visits his Muslim brother, he is in the harvested fruits of Paradise."
"22732","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Asim who said: I said to Abu al-Aliyah: Who is Thawban? He said: Freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who guarantees for me not to ask for anything and I guarantee Paradise for him? So Thawban said: I will. So he would not ask anyone for anything."
"22733","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Khalid from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Thawban from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When a man visits his brother, he is in the gardens of Paradise until he returns."
"22734","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Madan ibn Abi Talhah from Thawban that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows a funeral has a qirat, and whoever witnesses its burial has two qirats. It was said: What are the two qirats? He said: The smaller of them is like Uhud."
"22735","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Awzai saying: al-Walid ibn Hisham al-Muaiti narrated to me, Madan ibn Abi Talhah al-Yamuri narrated to me, he said: I met Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I said: Inform me of a deed I do by which Allah admits me to Paradise, or he said: I said: Of the most beloved deeds to Allah. So he fell silent, then I asked him a third time, so he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, so he said: Upon you is much prostration, for you do not prostrate to Allah a prostration except Allah raises you a degree by it and removes a sin from you by it."
"22736","Madan said: Then I met Abu al-Darda and asked him, so he said to me like what Thawban said to me."
"22737","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Salim from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright, and you will never encompass, and know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution except a believer."
"22738","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Abu Qilabah from one who narrated to him from Thawban who said: The Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who asks her husband for divorce without harm, the fragrance of Paradise is forbidden to her."
"22739","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Abu Qilabah from one who narrated to him from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best dinar is a dinar a man spends on his dependents, or on his mount in the cause of Allah, or on his companions in the cause of Allah."
"22740","Ismail narrated to us, Hisham informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Yaish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham from Madan from Abu al-Darda that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomited and broke the fast. He said: So I met Thawban in the mosque of Damascus and asked him about that, so he said: I poured ablution water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22741","Ismail narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma from Thawban that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man cupping in Ramadan and said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"22742","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Thawr from Rashid ibn Sad from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, and cold struck them. When they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they complained to him of what cold struck them, so he commanded them to wipe over headbands and warm socks."
"22743","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Salim from Madan from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and if he witnesses its burial he has two qirats, the qirat is like Uhud."
"22744","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Qays from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will accept for me one thing and I accept Paradise for him? He said: I said: I will. He said: Do not ask people for anything. So Thawban whip would fall while he was riding, and he would not say to anyone: Hand it to me, until he dismounted and took it himself."
"22745","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Isa from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Jad from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is deprived of provision by a sin he commits, nothing repels decree except supplication, and nothing increases lifespan except righteousness."
"22746","Waki narrated to us from Sharik from Ali ibn Zayd from Abu Qilabah from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the black banners coming from Khurasan, go to them, for among them is the caliph of Allah, al-Mahdi."
"22747","Waki narrated to us from al-Amash from Salim from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright toward Quraysh as long as they are upright toward you."
"22748","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Asim informed us from Abdullah ibn Zayd from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever visits a sick person remains in the harvest of Paradise. It was said: What is the harvest of Paradise? He said: Its fruits."
"22749","Yazid narrated to us from Hammam from Qatadah from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Madan ibn Abi Talhah from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever the soul leaves the body while he is free of three: arrogance, misappropriation, and debt, is in Paradise, or Paradise is assured for him."
"22750","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Muawiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah from Jubayr from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered a sacrifice, then said: O Thawban, prepare the meat of this sheep. He said: So I kept feeding him from it until he arrived in Madinah."
"22751","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Israel from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Thawban who said: When those who hoard gold and silver and do not spend it in the cause of Allah was revealed, we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, so some of his companions said: Concerning gold and silver what was revealed has come down, if only we knew which wealth is best we would take it. So he said: The best of it is a remembering tongue, a grateful heart, and a believing wife who helps him in his faith."
"22752","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ayyub from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I only fear for my nation the misleading leaders."
"22753","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from Ayyub from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I only fear for my nation the misleading leaders."
"22754","And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, folded the earth for me, or he said: My Lord folded the earth for me, so I saw its easts and its wests, and the dominion of my nation will reach what was folded for me of it, and I was given the two treasures, the red and the white, and I asked my Lord for my nation not to perish by a general famine, nor to set over them an enemy from other than themselves who would destroy them. And my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, said: O Muhammad, when I decree a decree it is not repelled, and Yunus said: It is not repelled. And I have given you for your nation not to destroy them by a general famine, nor to set over them an enemy from other than themselves who would destroy them, even if all from around it gather against them, until some of them enslave others. And I only fear for my nation the misleading leaders."
"22755","And when the sword is placed in my nation, it will not be lifted from them until the Day of Resurrection."
"22756","And the Hour will not come until tribes of my nation join the polytheists, until tribes of my nation worship idols."
"22757","And there will be in my nation thirty liars, each of them claiming he is a prophet, and I am the Seal of the Prophets, no prophet after me."
"22758","And a group of my nation will remain upon the truth, manifest, those who oppose them will not harm them until the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes."
"22759","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salim and Abu Bakr ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi narrated to us from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi from Luqman ibn Amir al-Wusabi from Abd al-Ala ibn Adi al-Bahrani from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Two groups of my nation Allah has protected from the Fire: a group that raids India, and a group that will be with Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon him."
"22760","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, Marzuq Abu Abdullah al-Himsi narrated to us, Abu Asma al-Rahabi narrated to us from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is near that nations will call one another against you from every horizon, as eaters call one another to their dish. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, is it from fewness among us that day? He said: You that day are many, but you will be scum like the scum of the flood. He will remove fear from the hearts of your enemy, and place weakness in your hearts. He said: We said: What is weakness? He said: Love of life and hatred of death."
"22761","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Zayd ibn Sallam narrated to me that his grandfather narrated to him that Abu Asma narrated to him that Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to him that the daughter of Hubayrah entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with gold rings on her hand called fatah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began tapping her hand with a small stick with him, saying to her: Would it please you that Allah put rings of Fire on your hand? So she went to Fatimah and complained to her of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did to her. He said: And I went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he stood behind the door, and when he sought permission he stood behind the door. He said: So Fatimah said to her: Look at this chain that Abu Hasan gifted me, and on her hand was a chain of gold. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: O Fatimah, is it just that people say Fatimah daughter of Muhammad with a chain of Fire on your hand? Then he rebuked her severely, then left and did not sit. So she ordered the chain to be sold, and bought a slave with its price and freed him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that, he said takbir and said: Praise be to Allah who saved Fatimah from the Fire."
"22762","al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Ayyash, narrated to us from Layth from Abu al-Khattab from Abu Zurah from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the briber, the bribed, and the intermediary, meaning the one who walks between them."
"22763","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Maymun Abu Muhammad al-Muzani al-Tamimi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makhzumi narrated to us from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is pleased with delay in lifespan and increase in provision, let him uphold his kinship."
"22764","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Maymun informed us, Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A servant seeks the pleasure of Allah and continues in that, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says to Jibril: So-and-so, My servant, seeks to please Me, indeed My mercy is upon him. So Jibril says: The mercy of Allah upon so-and-so, and the bearers of the Throne say it, and those around them say it, until the people of the seven heavens say it, then it descends to him on earth."
"22765","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Maymun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not harm the servants of Allah, do not shame them, and do not seek their faults, for whoever seeks the fault of his Muslim brother, Allah seeks his fault until He disgraces him in his house."
"22766","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Ayyub from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A group of my nation will remain upon the truth, manifest, those who fail them will not harm them until the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes."
"22767","Yunus and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us from Ayyub from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma from Thawban, I do not know except he raised it, Affan said: From Thawban, he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: One who visits a sick person is in the harvest of Paradise, and Ibn Mahdi did not doubt in it."
"22768","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who guarantees for me one thing and I guarantee Paradise for him? He said: I said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do not ask people for anything. He said: So the whip of Thawban would fall while he was on his camel, so he would kneel it until he took it, and would not say to anyone: Hand it to me."
"22769","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Ayyub from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best dinar a man spends is on his dependents, then on himself, then in the cause of Allah, then on his companions in the cause of Allah. Abu Qilabah said: So he begins with dependents."
"22770","And Sulayman ibn Harb said, and he did not raise it: A dinar a man spends on his mount in the cause of Allah."
"22771","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us from Khalid from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a Muslim visits his Muslim brother, he remains in the harvest of Paradise until he returns."
"22772","Abu Ishaq al-Talaqani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from al-Awzai, Abu Ammar narrated to me, Abu Asma al-Rahabi narrated to me, Thawban narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to finish his prayer, would say: I seek the forgiveness of Allah three times, then say: O Allah, You are Peace and from You is peace, blessed are You, Possessor of Majesty and Honor."
"22773","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah from Salim from Madan from Thawban that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am at the side of my Hawd on the Day of Resurrection, driving people from it for the people of Yemen, and I strike them with my staff until it pours forth from them. He said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is its extent? He said: From my place to Oman, two spouts flow into it, extending it."
"22774","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by al-Baqi on the eighteenth night past of Ramadan by a man cupping, and said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"22775","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Hisham narrated to me, Madan narrated to me, he said: I said to Thawban, freed slave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Narrate to us a hadith by which Allah benefits us. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No servant prostrates to Allah a prostration except Allah raises him a degree by it and removes a sin from him by it."
"22776","al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Dhimari from Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever fasts Ramadan, a month is ten months, and fasting six days after Fitr, that completes the fasting of the year."
"22777","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from Abdullah ibn Isa from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Jad al-Ashjai from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Nothing repels decree except supplication, nothing increases lifespan except righteousness, and a servant is deprived of provision by a sin he commits."
"22778","Ali ibn Ayyash and Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us, they said: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Be upright, you will succeed, and the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution except a believer. And Isam said: Nor preserves."
"22779","al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Habib ibn Salih from Yazid ibn Shurayh al-Hadrami from Abu Hayy al-Muadhdhin from Thawban from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: It is not lawful for a Muslim man to look inside the house of a man until he seeks permission, for if he looks he has entered, nor to lead people and single himself out with supplication apart from them, for if he does he has betrayed them, nor to pray while restraining until he relieves himself."
"22780","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad, meaning al-Khattabi, narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us from Habib ibn Salih from Yazid ibn Shurayh, and he mentioned its meaning with its chain."
"22781","al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Ubaydullah ibn Ubayd al-Kalai from Zuhayr from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr from his father Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: For every forgetfulness are two prostrations after he gives salam."
"22782","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Damdam ibn Zurah who said: Shurayh ibn Ubayd said: Thawban fell ill in Hims, over which was Abdullah ibn Qurt al-Azdi, and he did not visit him. So a man of the Kalaites entered upon Thawban visiting, so Thawban said to him: Can you write? He said: Yes. He said: Write. So he wrote: To the trusted Abdullah ibn Qurt, from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): As for what follows, if Musa and Isa had a freed slave in your presence, you would visit him. Then he folded the letter and said to him: Will you deliver it to him? He said: Yes. So the man went with his letter and gave it to Ibn Qurt. When he read it, he stood up in alarm. People said: What is wrong with him, has something happened? So he went to Thawban until he entered upon him, and visited him, and sat with him a while, then stood. So Thawban took his cloak and said: Sit until I narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I heard him saying: Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise with no reckoning upon them nor punishment, with every thousand seventy thousand."
"22783","al-Hasan ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us from Muawiyah from Utbah Abu Umayyah al-Dimashqi from Abu Sallam al-Aswad from Thawban that he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over the leather socks and over the khimar, then the turban."
"22784","Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abdullah ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us from Said ibn Abi Arubah from Qatadah from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Madan ibn Abi Talhah from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever asks for charity while rich without need of it, it will be a mark on his face on the Day of Resurrection."
"22785","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu al-Zahiriyyah narrated to me from Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered a sacrifice of his, then said to me: O Thawban, prepare the meat of this sheep. He said: So I kept feeding him from it until he arrived in Madinah."
"22786","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Asim, meaning al-Ahwal, informed us from Abdullah ibn Zayd, meaning Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever visits a sick person remains in the harvest of Paradise. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the harvest of Paradise? He said: Its fruits."
"22787","Yazid ibn Harun and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Qays from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will accept for me one thing, I accept Paradise for him? He said: I said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do not ask people for anything. He said: So perhaps the whip of Thawban would fall while he was on his camel, and he would not ask anyone to hand it to him until he dismounted to it and took it."
"22788","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mina from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Muawiyah from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who guarantees for me a trait and I guarantee Paradise for him? And he mentioned its meaning."
"22789","Rawh narrated to us, Marzuq Abu Abdullah al-Shami narrated to us, Said, a man of the people of Sham, narrated to us, Thawban narrated to us from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When fever strikes one of you, and fever is a portion of the Fire, let him extinguish it from himself with cold water, facing a flowing river, facing the flow of water, saying: In the name of Allah, O Allah heal Your servant and confirm Your Messenger, after Fajr prayer before sunrise, immersing himself in it three immersions for three days. If he does not recover in three, then five, and if he does not recover in five, then seven, and if he does not recover in seven, then nine, for it hardly exceeds nine, by the permission of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"22790","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Madan ibn Abi Talhah from Thawban that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am at the side of my Hawd, driving it for the people of Yemen, striking with my staff until it pours forth over them. He was asked about its width, so he said: From my place to Oman. And he was asked about its drink, so he said: Whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, two spouts branch into it, extending it from Paradise, one of gold and the other of silver."
"22791","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, they said: Said narrated to us from Qatadah from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Madan from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever the soul leaves the body while he is free of three enters Paradise: arrogance, misappropriation, and debt."
"22792","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah, and Bahz said: Qatadah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, Bahz said: From Salim from Madan from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever the soul leaves the body while he is free of three enters Paradise: misappropriation and debt, Bahz said: And arrogance."
"22793","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Said narrated to us from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"22794","Bahz narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Abi al-Sumayt narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad al-Ghatafani from Madan ibn Abi Talhah from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am at the side of my Hawd, driving people from it for the people of Yemen, I strike them with my staff until it pours forth over them, and two spouts flow into it, one of silver and the other of gold, between Busra and Sanaa, or between Aylah and Makkah, or he said: From this place of mine to Oman."
"22795","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Makhul informed me that an old man of the tribe informed him that Thawban, freed slave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"22796","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, and Rawh narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma al-Rahabi who said: Thawban, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was walking in al-Baqi in Ramadan, he saw a man cupping and said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"22797","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, Hassan ibn Atiyyah narrated to me that Abu Kabshah al-Saluli narrated to him that he heard Thawban saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be correct and near, work and choose the best, and know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution except a believer."
"22798","Affan narrated to us, Hammam and Aban narrated to us, they said: Qatadah narrated to us from Salim from Madan from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever the soul leaves the body while he is free of three enters Paradise: arrogance, debt, and misappropriation."
"22799","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Shubah from Qatadah from Salim from Madan from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and if he witnesses its burial he has two qirats, the qirat is like Uhud."
"22800","Waki and Yala narrated to us, they said: al-Amash narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright, and you will never encompass, and know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution except a believer."
"22801","Waki narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Murrah told me, from his father, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jaad, from Thawban, who said: When what was revealed concerning silver and gold was revealed, they said: So what wealth should we take? Umar said: I will learn that for you for you. He said: So he urged his camel on and caught up with him, and I was behind him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, what wealth should we take? He said: Let one of you take a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, and a wife who helps him in the matter of the Hereafter."
"22802","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Jaad, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed the servant is deprived of provision by the sin he commits, and nothing repels the decree except supplication, and nothing increases in lifespan except righteousness."
"22803","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One who visits the sick is in the harvested fruits of Paradise."
"22804","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, who said, and he mentioned Abu Asma and mentioned Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any woman who asks her husband for divorce without any harm, the fragrance of Paradise is forbidden to her."
"22805","Abdul-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Hisham, meaning Ibn Abi Abdullah, narrated to us, and Ibn Jafar, meaning Ghundar, narrated to us: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jaad, from Maadan ibn Abi Talhah, from Thawban, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it, he has a qirat, and if he witnesses its burial, he has two qirats. They said: And what are the two qirats? He said: The smaller of them is like Uhud."
"22806","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jaad, who said: It was said to Thawban: Narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: You would lie about me. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There is no Muslim who prostrates to Allah a prostration except that Allah raises him a degree by it and removes a sin from him by it."
"22807","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Judi, from Balj, from Abu Shaybah al-Mahri, who said, and he was the storyteller of the people in Constantinople, who said: It was said to Thawban: Narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, vomit and break his fast. Hajjaj said: Constantinople."
"22808","Yunus narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadh-dha, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Indeed the Muslim, when he visits his Muslim brother, remains in the harvested fruits of Paradise until he returns."
"22809","Ismail narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from one who narrated to him, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One who visits the sick is in the harvested fruits of Paradise until he returns."
"22810","Abdul-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Indeed the Muslim, when he visits his brother, remains in the harvested fruits of Paradise until he returns."
"22811","Abdul-Wahhab narrated to us: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jaad al-Ghatafani, from Maadan ibn Abi Talhah al-Yamuri, from Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Indeed I will be at the side of the Hawd on the Day of Resurrection, driving people away from it for the people of Yemen; I will strike them with my stick until it flows upon them. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about its width, and he said: From this station of mine to Oman. And he was asked about its drink, and he said: Whiter than milk and sweeter than honey; two spouts pour into it, extending to it from Paradise, one of gold and the other of silver."
"22812","Abdul-Wahhab narrated to us: Hisham ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim, from Maadan, from Thawban, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"22813","He said: Hasan ibn Musa and Husayn ibn Muhammad told me, both saying: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, who said: Abu Qilabah al-Jarmi told me that he was informed that Shaddad ibn Aws, while he was walking with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in al-Baqi, passed by a man being cupped after eighteen nights of Ramadan had passed, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"22814","Hasan ibn Musa and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, both saying: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, who said: And Abu Qilabah informed me that Abu Asma ar-Rahabi narrated to him that Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed him that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"22815","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ashath as-Sanani, from Abu Asma ar-Rahabi, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the Muslim visits his brother, he walks in the harvested fruits of Paradise until he returns."
"22816","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah, or: indeed my Lord, folded the earth for me, its easts and its wests, and indeed the dominion of my ummah will reach what was folded for me of it, and I was given the two treasures, the red and the white, and indeed I asked my Lord for my ummah that He not destroy it with a general famine, and that He not set over them an enemy from other than themselves who would exterminate their stock, until some of them take others captive and some of them destroy others, even if those from between its regions gathered against them, or he said: those in its regions."
"22817","Lo, indeed I fear for my ummah the misguiding imams."
"22818","And when the sword is placed in my ummah, it will not be lifted from it until the Day of Resurrection."
"22819","And the Hour will not come until tribes of my ummah join the polytheists, and until tribes of my ummah worship idols."
"22820","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, dictating it to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best dinar is a dinar a man spends on his dependents, and a dinar he spends on his mount in the path of Allah. He said: Then Abu Qilabah said on his own part: dutifulness to dependents. He said: And what man is greater in reward than a man who spends on his dependents, young ones, whom Allah makes independent through him."
"22821","Affan narrated to us: Aban narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jaad, from Maadan ibn Abi Talhah, from Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever witnesses its burial has two qirats. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and what are the two qirats? He said: The smaller of them is like Uhud."
"22822","Abdul-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, who said: Said was asked about a man who follows a funeral, what reward he has, so he informed us, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jaad, from Maadan ibn Abi Talhah, from Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and if he witnesses its burial, he has two qirats. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about that qirat, and he said: Like Uhud."
